From 5388ab67724394ffb2db4a269a1c4e96d5d22102 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gtguerreiro-max <295622337+gtguerreiro-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:30:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: Xenia canary's game patches beside a module
 (<path>.patch.toml)

Once a XEX module is loaded (its title update applied), a patch file beside it in Xenia canary's
format (its game-patches repository) is applied to the module's memory: the patches whose
is_enabled is true, when the file's title id is the module's and one of its hashes is the module
hash as Xenia canary computes it (UserModule::CalculateHash: XXH3-64 over the code pages, the
import thunks rewritten `sc 2; blr; nop; nop`). Codegen and the title load the module the same
way, so a code patch is in the recompiled code and a data patch in the title's memory.

Every module load logs its title and module hash. Write types and values as Xenia canary's
PatchDB reads them: be8, be16, be32, be64, f32, f64, string, u16string and array.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
